    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/420765633/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """I suppose my remarks on the picture were not as edifying as they might have been. It is really too silly to fight. Why on earth should we?
Thursday Feb. 28. ‘95 Fiesole
Awoke to a fierce snow-storm! But it was gone, and all the snow, too, by afternoon. Emily and Miss Anstruther Thompson came to lunch, and Bernhard talked to us enchantingly about the early Sienese. We had a nice walk, and I finished the Lafenestre in the evening. Mrs. Jack Gardner wrote that she would take 2 Peruzzis Bernhard wrote to her about, thereby causing us to rejoice, for we are low in funds and this means about £70. """^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 107 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1894-95> .

